From: Paul Philippov <paul@themactep.com>
Subject: [PATCH] nvmem: jz4780-efuse: add the T41

The T41 efuse is the T31 block at 0x13540000: EFUCTRL/EFUCFG/
EFUSTATE and the 32-byte data window are the same, and the serial
number lives in the raw rows the userspace helpers read at +0x200.
Bind it so the driver ungates T41_CLK_EFUSE and programs the read
timing; without that the serial and SoC-type reads come back empty
and the hostname loses its serial-derived suffix.

Signed-off-by: Paul Philippov <paul@themactep.com>
---
--- a/drivers/nvmem/jz4780-efuse.c
+++ b/drivers/nvmem/jz4780-efuse.c
@@ -232,6 +232,7 @@
 static const struct of_device_id jz4780_efuse_match[] = {
 	{ .compatible = "ingenic,jz4780-efuse", .data = &jz4780_efuse_soc_data },
 	{ .compatible = "ingenic,t31-efuse",    .data = &t31_efuse_soc_data    },
+	{ .compatible = "ingenic,t41-efuse",    .data = &t31_efuse_soc_data    },
 	{ /* sentinel */ },
 };
 MODULE_DEVICE_TABLE(of, jz4780_efuse_match);
